\section{Global State Vector Construction}

The global state vector is defined as the direct sum of all engine
states:
\begin{equation}
  \Psi_{\text{global}}
  =
  \Psi_{\text{BRE}}
  \oplus
  \Psi_{\text{APEX}}
  \oplus
  \Psi_{\text{TASSE}}
  \oplus
  \Psi_{\text{Mnemosyne}}.
\end{equation}

Each component resides on its own manifold:
\begin{align}
  \Psi_{\text{BRE}} &\in \mathcal{M}_{\text{hemo}}, \\
  \Psi_{\text{APEX}} &\in \mathcal{M}_{\text{tensor}}, \\
  \Psi_{\text{TASSE}} &\in \mathcal{M}_{\text{astro}}, \\
  \Psi_{\text{Mnemosyne}} &\in \mathcal{M}_{\text{neuro}}.
\end{align}

The suprakernel manifold is:
\begin{equation}
  \mathcal{M}_{\text{supr}}
  =
  \mathcal{M}_{\text{hemo}}
  \times
  \mathcal{M}_{\text{tensor}}
  \times
  \mathcal{M}_{\text{astro}}
  \times
  \mathcal{M}_{\text{neuro}}.
\end{equation}

