\section{Orthogonal Projection Operator}

When invariants are violated, the suprakernel applies the correction
operator:
\begin{equation}
  \Phi_{\text{control}}(\Psi)
  =
  \operatorname{Proj}_{\mathcal{I}}(\Psi),
\end{equation}
where $\operatorname{Proj}_{\mathcal{I}}$ is the orthogonal projection
onto the invariant manifold.

Projection is defined as:
\begin{equation}
  \operatorname{Proj}_{\mathcal{I}}(\Psi)
  =
  \arg\min_{\Psi' \in \mathcal{I}}
  \lVert \Psi' - \Psi \rVert_2.
\end{equation}

